---
description: "Twig templating rules and best practices for Twig version 3"
globs: *.twig
alwaysApply: false
---

## General

- Use Twig version 3.x
- Use modern Twig syntax and features.
- Follow Twig best practices and conventions.
- Variables and macros follow camelCase format.

## Code Quality

- Use meaningful variable names
- Add comments for complex logic
- Follow consistent formatting
- Maintain clean, readable template structure

## Indentation

- Use 4 spaces for indentation (no tabs)
- Maintain consistent indentation throughout
- Align Twig tags with HTML structure

## Good code examples

### Template Structure

```twig
{# Good: Proper Twig structure with indentation #}
{% extends "base.twig" %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="page-header">
        <h1 class="page-header__title">
            {{ page.title }}
        </h1>
        {% if page.subtitle %}
            <p class="page-header__subtitle">
                {{ page.subtitle }}
            </p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endblock %}
```

### Variable Usage

```twig
{# Good: Safe variable access #}
{{ page.title|default('Default Title') }}

{# Good: Conditional content #}
{% if page.description %}
    <p class="content__description">
        {{ page.description }}
    </p>
{% endif %}

{# Good: Loops with proper structure #}
{% for item in items %}
    <div class="item">
        <h3 class="item__title">
            {{ item.title }}
        </h3>
        <p class="item__description">
            {{ item.description }}
        </p>
    </div>
{% endfor %}
```

### Template Inheritance

```twig
{# Good: Base template structure #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ site.language|default('en') }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>
        {{ page.title }}
    </title>
</head>
<body>
    {% block content %}{% endblock %}
    {% block sidebar %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
```

### Includes and Macros

```twig
{# Good: Include structure #}
{% include 'components/header.twig' with {
    'title': page.title,
    'navigation': navigation
} %}

{# Good: Macro definition #}
{% macro button(text, url, class) %}
    {% set class = 'Button ' ~ class %}
    <a href="{{ url }}" class="{{ class|trim }}">
        {{ text }}
    </a>
{% endmacro %}

{# Good: Macro usage #}
{% import 'macros/buttons.twig' as buttons %}
{{ buttons.button('Learn More', '/about', 'Button--primary') }}
```

### Filters and Functions

```twig
{# Good: Using filters #}
{{ page.content|striptags|slice(0, 150) }}...

{# Good: Date formatting #}
{{ page.date|date('F j, Y') }}

{# Good: URL generation #}
<a href="{{ url('page', {'slug': page.slug}) }}">
    {{ page.title }}
</a>

{# Good: Image handling #}
{% do image.resie(800, 600) %}
{% do image.lazy() %}
{% do image.alt.default('Default alt') %}
{{ image.tag }}
```

### Conditional Logic

```twig
{# Good: Complex conditionals #}
{% if page.featured and page.category == 'news' %}
    <div class="featured-news">
        <h2 class="featured-news__title">
            {{ page.title }}
        </h2>
    </div>
{% elseif page.category == 'services' %}
    <div class="service-content">
        <h2 class="service-content__title">
            {{ page.title }}
        </h2>
    </div>
{% else %}
    <div class="standard-content">
        <h2 class="standard-content__title">
            {{ page.title }}
        </h2>
    </div>
{% endif %}
```

### Loops and Iteration

```twig
{# Good: Loop with index #}
{% for service in services %}
    <div class="Service{% if loop.last %} Service--last{% endif %}">
        <h3 class="Service-title">
            {{ service.title }}
        </h3>
        <p class="Service-description">
            {{ service.description }}
        </p>
        {% if service.features %}
            <ul class="Service-features">
                {% for feature in service.features %}
                    <li class="Service-feature">
                        {{ feature }}
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endfor %}
```

### Comments and Documentation

```twig
{# Good: Template comments #}
{#
    Header component
    Displays site navigation and branding
    Variables: title, navigation, logo
#}
<header class="header">
    <div class="header__brand">
        <a href="{{ url('home') }}" class="header__logo">
            {{ site.name }}
        </a>
    </div>

    {# Navigation menu #}
    <nav class="header__nav">
        {% include 'components/navigation.twig' %}
    </nav>
</header>
```

### Security Best Practices

```twig
{# Good: Safe output #}
{{ user_input|escape }}

{# Good: Safe attributes #}
<div class="content" data-id="{{ item.id|escape('html_attr') }}">
    {{ item.content|raw }}
</div>

{# Good: URL safety #}
<a href="{{ url|escape('url') }}">
    {{ link_text }}
</a>
```

### Performance Considerations

```twig
{# Good: Conditional loading #}
{% if page.images %}
    {% include 'components/image-gallery.twig' with {
        'images': page.images
    } %}
{% endif %}

{# Good: Caching considerations #}
{# Cache this block for 1 hour #}
{% cache 'page-content' ~ page.id, 3600 %}
    <div class="page-content">
        {{ page.content }}
    </div>
{% endcache %}
```
